# The complete public command surface remains visible and stable.

```console
$ lllm --help
Send stateless prompts through lithos-llm

Usage: lllm [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]...
       lllm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  prompt   Send one stateless prompt
  probe    Test whether a model can serve requests now
  resolve  Print the canonical route without making a request
  models   List and search the built-in model catalog

Options:
      --verbose         Log library diagnostics to standard error. RUST_LOG overrides this
      --catalog <PATH>  Add a local TOML catalog overlay for this process. Can be repeated
  -h, --help            Print help
  -V, --version         Print version

Examples:
  lllm "Explain this code"
  lllm -m anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 "Hello"
  lllm probe --model-query sonnet
  lllm resolve --model-query sonnet
  lllm models --adapter-compiled

$ lllm prompt --help
Send one stateless prompt

Usage: lllm prompt [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]...

Arguments:
  [PROMPT]...  Prompt text. Multiple values are joined with one space

Options:
      --no-stream
          Do not stream the response
  -u, --usage
          Print model, token, cost, and latency usage to standard error
  -m, --model <MODEL>
          Use this model selector unchanged
  -q, --model-query <MODEL_QUERY>
          Search compiled models. Every repeated term must match
  -s, --system <SYSTEM>
          Add a system message
      --verbose
          Log library diagnostics to standard error. RUST_LOG overrides this
      --catalog <PATH>
          Add a local TOML catalog overlay for this process. Can be repeated
  -f, --fragment <PATH>
          Add a local UTF-8 file as user context. Can be repeated
      --system-fragment <PATH>
          Add a local UTF-8 file to the system message. Can be repeated
      --max-output-tokens <MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS>
          Limit the number of tokens generated by the model
      --temperature <TEMPERATURE>
          Set the sampling temperature
      --top-p <TOP_P>
          Set nucleus sampling probability
      --reasoning-effort <REASONING_EFFORT>
          Set the model reasoning effort [possible values: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max]
      --speed <SPEED>
          Select a speed and price tier [possible values: fast, balanced, economical]
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Call timeout. Use an explicit unit, for example 500ms, 30s, or 2m
      --stop <STOP>
          Stop generation when this text occurs. Can be repeated
      --cache-key <CACHE_KEY>
          Route compatible calls to the same provider cache entry
      --no-cache
          Disable provider prompt caching for this call
      --metadata <KEY=VALUE>
          Add request metadata as KEY=VALUE. Can be repeated
  -o, --option <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a provider option as KEY=VALUE. Can be repeated
  -a, --attachment <ATTACHMENT>
          Attach a URL or file. Use - to read one attachment from standard input
      --attachment-type <SOURCE> <MEDIA_TYPE>
          Attach a source with an explicit media type
      --json
          Emit a versioned JSON request and response envelope
      --json-object
          Ask the provider for a JSON object
      --schema <SCHEMA>
          Ask for one structured object. Use shorthand, JSON, or @PATH
      --schema-multi <SCHEMA_MULTI>
          Ask for an array of structured objects. Use shorthand, JSON, or @PATH
      --schema-name <SCHEMA_NAME>
          Name used for --schema or --schema-multi. Defaults to response
  -x, --extract
          Print the first complete fenced code block
      --extract-last
          Print the last complete fenced code block [aliases: --xl]
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ lllm resolve --help
Print the canonical route without making a request

Usage: lllm resolve [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -m, --model <MODEL>              Use this model selector unchanged
  -q, --model-query <MODEL_QUERY>  Search compiled models. Every repeated term must match
      --verbose                    Log library diagnostics to standard error. RUST_LOG overrides this
      --catalog <PATH>             Add a local TOML catalog overlay for this process. Can be repeated
  -h, --help                       Print help

$ lllm probe --help
Test whether a model can serve requests now

Usage: lllm probe [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -m, --model <MODEL>
          Use this model selector unchanged
  -q, --model-query <MODEL_QUERY>
          Search compiled models. Every repeated term must match
      --tools
          Exercise a fixed add-tool exchange instead of one short prompt
      --reasoning-effort <REASONING_EFFORT>
          Set the model reasoning effort [possible values: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max]
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Bound the whole probe. Defaults to 30s, or 90s with --tools
      --verbose
          Log library diagnostics to standard error. RUST_LOG overrides this
      --catalog <PATH>
          Add a local TOML catalog overlay for this process. Can be repeated
      --json
          Emit a versioned JSON probe report
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ lllm models --help
List and search the built-in model catalog

Usage: lllm models [OPTIONS] [QUERY]...

Arguments:
  [QUERY]...  Terms that every listed model must match

Options:
      --json                     Emit the documented JSON model-list shape
      --adapter-compiled         Show only models whose provider adapter is compiled into this CLI
      --provider <PROVIDER>      Show only models from this provider ID or alias
      --capability <CAPABILITY>  Show only models with this capability [possible values: text, images, audio, documents, tools, structured-output, reasoning, caching, sampling]
      --configured               Show only models whose credentials are configured
      --verbose                  Log library diagnostics to standard error. RUST_LOG overrides this
      --catalog <PATH>           Add a local TOML catalog overlay for this process. Can be repeated
      --default                  Show only the effective default model
  -h, --help                     Print help

$ lllm --version
lllm 0.1.0

```
